done at set intervals, say once a month or once every two months,
and on a set of fresh tapes that is saved forever.  After a level
0, dumps of active file systems are taken on a daily basis, using
a  modified  Tower of Hanoi algorithm, with this sequence of dump
levels: 3 2 5 4 7 6 9 8 9 9 ...  For the daily dumps,  it  should
be  possible to use a fixed number of tapes for each day, used on
a weekly basis.  Each week, a level 1  dump  is  taken,  and  the
daily Hanoi sequence repeats beginning with 3.  For weekly dumps,
another  fixed  set of tapes per dumped file system is used, also
on a cyclical basis.  After several months or so, the  daily  and
weekly  tapes  should get rotated out of the dump cycle and fresh
